{"step_index":271,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-15T09:04:46Z","model":"gemini-3.8-flash-high","input_tokens":5468,"cache_read_tokens":203468,"output_tokens":1491,"content":"The first-visit lag issue has been resolved. Here is the technical breakdown of what was causing the lag and the optimizations applied:\n\n---\n\n### 🔍 Root Causes of the Initial Load Lag\n\n1. **Uncompressed HTML & Missing Route Compression**:\n   The server skipped compression whenever a visitor opened the homepage (`/`) or clean route directories (`/about/`, `/contact/`) because the URL lacked a file extension. The full 94 KB HTML was sent raw, delaying First Contentful Paint.\n2. **212 KB AI Chatbot Executing During Critical First Render**:\n   [quick-actions.js](file:///Users/ravi/Desktop/kezza_clinic-main/frontend/js/quick-actions.js) was immediately downloading and parsing `kezza-ai.min.js` (212 KB of minified JS, regexes, and voice synthesis routines) within milliseconds of page load, choking the main thread before the browser could paint the hero section.\n3. **5 Separate Render-Blocking Stylesheets in `<head>`**:\n   The browser had to download and parse 5 separate CSS files (`bundle-home.min.css`, `genuine-reviews.css`, `site-quality.css`, `upgrades-pro.css`, and `fa-subset.min.css`) totaling over 370 KB before rendering a single pixel.\n4. **Third-Party Script & Analytics Network Contention**:\n   Google Tag Manager and Google Analytics scripts were executed synchronously at the very start of `<head>`, competing with critical CSS, fonts, and hero imagery for network bandwidth.\n5. **Immediate Off-Screen Network & Animation Tasks**:\n   `kezza-reviews.min.js` was immediately dispatching a fetch for `genuine-reviews.json` to populate cards that are 1,000 lines down the page, while `scroll-3d.js` and `pro-animations.js` started unthrottled continuous RAF loops and DOM-wide query selectors on `DOMContentLoaded`.\n\n---\n\n### ⚡ Key Optimizations Implemented\n\n#### 1. Server-Side Delivery & Caching ([server.js](file:///Users/ravi/Desktop/kezza_clinic-main/server.js))\n* **Brotli (`br`) & Gzip with In-Memory Cache**:\n  Added on-the-fly Brotli and Gzip compression with an in-memory buffer cache for all compressible routes (`/`, directories, `.html`, `.css`, `.js`, `.json`, `.svg`). \n  * Homepage payload dropped **81%** (from **94.3 KB down to 18.0 KB**).\n  * Main CSS bundle dropped from **292 KB down to 50 KB**.\n  * Repeat and concurrent requests now return in **~2 ms**.\n* **Smart Browser Caching**:\n  * Set `Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate` for HTML to enable instant 304 conditional validation via ETags.\n  * Set `Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable` for all version-hashed production CSS/JS bundles and static media.\n\n#### 2. Critical Path Optimization ([frontend/index.html](file:///Users/ravi/Desktop/kezza_clinic-main/frontend/index.html))\n* **Non-Blocking FontAwesome & Upgrades CSS**:\n  Converted `fa-subset.min.css` and `upgrades-pro.css` to asynchronous preloading (`rel=\"preload\"` with `onload=\"this.rel='stylesheet'\"` and `<noscript>` fallback), eliminating render-blocking delays.\n* **Consolidated Stylesheets**:\n  Merged `genuine-reviews.css` and `site-quality.css` directly into `bundle-home.min.css` via [tools/css-bundles.json](file:///Users/ravi/Desktop/kezza_clinic-main/tools/css-bundles.json) and rebuilt the bundles.\n* **Deferred Analytics & Fallbacks**:\n  * Wrapped GTM and Google Analytics in an idle-callback loader so they initialize only after first paint.\n  * Added `defer` attributes to `media-fallbacks.min.js`, `whatsapp-followup.min.js`, and `booking-modal.min.js`.\n\n#### 3. Main-Thread Optimization & Progressive Hydration\n* **Progressive Loading for AI Chatbot ([quick-actions.js](file:///Users/ravi/Desktop/kezza_clinic-main/frontend/js/quick-actions.js))**:\n  The 212 KB `kezza-ai.min.js` now loads either upon first user interaction (`pointerdown`, `scroll`, `touchstart`, or clicking the chat consultant button) or when the browser enters an idle state (after 3.5s), keeping the main thread 100% free during startup.\n* **Viewport-Based Lazy Loading for Reviews ([kezza-reviews.js](file:///Users/ravi/Desktop/kezza_clinic-main/frontend/js/kezza-reviews.js))**:\n  Reviews are now fetched via an `IntersectionObserver` when the user actually scrolls near the reviews section.\n* **Idle Scheduling for 3D & Micro-Interactions ([scroll-3d.js](file:///Users/ravi/Desktop/kezza_clinic-main/frontend/js/scroll-3d.js) & [pro-animations.js](file:///Users/ravi/Desktop/kezza_clinic-main/frontend/js/pro-animations.js))**:\n  Throttled mousemove triggers to requestAnimationFrame and deferred card tilt and count-up calculations until after the initial paint.\n\n---\n\n### 📊 Verification & Status\n* **Test Suite:** `npm test` passed with **0 errors, 0 warnings, 119 pages valid**.\n* **Assets Verified:** All 23 production assets return `HTTP 200 OK` with proper compression headers.\n* **Live Server:** Running at [http://localhost:3001](http://localhost:3001)."}
